@lang en
-- Tests of ie-general.l4: ss 2(1), 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 11, 12, 13 and 14(1).
-- Each expected value was read off the quoted section (the conjunctions and disjunctions are the text's own: "and", "or", "unless", "except in so far as").
-- For each rule the tests vary one input at a time, so that every input is shown to matter, and the boundary between two branches is tested on both sides.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ie-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `ie-general`

§ `Helpers`

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
      f IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about a document`
`a document with` a b c d e f MEANS
    `Facts about a document` WITH
        `it is an Act of the Oireachtas`                                                                                        IS a
        `it is a statute that was in force in Saorstat Eireann immediately before the Constitution came into operation`         IS b
        `it continued in force by virtue of Article 50 of the Constitution`                                                     IS c
        `it is an order, regulation, rule, bye-law, warrant, licence, certificate, direction, notice, guideline or other like document` IS d
        `it was made, issued, granted or otherwise created by or under an Act or such an instrument`                            IS e
        `it is a portion of an Act or of a statutory instrument`                                                                IS f

§ `Section 2(1): "Act"`

#ASSERT     `is an Act` (`a document with` TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT     `is an Act` (`a document with` FALSE TRUE  TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `is an Act` (`a document with` FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `is an Act` (`a document with` FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `is an Act` (`a document with` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `is an Act` (`a document with` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  TRUE  TRUE)

§ `Section 2(1): "statutory instrument"`

#ASSERT     `is a statutory instrument` (`a document with` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  TRUE  FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `is a statutory instrument` (`a document with` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `is a statutory instrument` (`a document with` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `is a statutory instrument` (`a document with` TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§ `Section 2(1): "enactment" is an Act, a statutory instrument, or a portion of either`

#ASSERT     `is an enactment` (`a document with` TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT     `is an enactment` (`a document with` FALSE TRUE  TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT     `is an enactment` (`a document with` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  TRUE  FALSE)
#ASSERT     `is an enactment` (`a document with` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `is an enactment` (`a document with` FALSE TRUE  FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `is an enactment` (`a document with` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§ `Section 2(1): "repeal" includes revoke, rescind, abrogate or cancel; the list is open, so another word is not answered`

#ASSERT `the word is a repeal within the Act` repeal
#ASSERT `the word is a repeal within the Act` revoke
#ASSERT `the word is a repeal within the Act` rescind
#ASSERT `the word is a repeal within the Act` abrogate
#ASSERT `the word is a repeal within the Act` cancel
#ASSERT REFUSED `the word is a repeal within the Act` `some other word` BECAUSE "section 2(1) says that repeal includes the listed words, so whether another word is a repeal is not answered"

§ `Section 4(1): a provision applies unless the contrary intention appears in this Act, in the enactment, or (where relevant) in the Act under which it is made`

#ASSERT     `a provision of this Act applies to an enactment` (`Where a contrary intention appears` WITH `in this Act` IS FALSE, `in the enactment itself` IS FALSE, `in the Act under which it is made` IS NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `a provision of this Act applies to an enactment` (`Where a contrary intention appears` WITH `in this Act` IS TRUE,  `in the enactment itself` IS FALSE, `in the Act under which it is made` IS NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `a provision of this Act applies to an enactment` (`Where a contrary intention appears` WITH `in this Act` IS FALSE, `in the enactment itself` IS TRUE,  `in the Act under which it is made` IS NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `a provision of this Act applies to an enactment` (`Where a contrary intention appears` WITH `in this Act` IS FALSE, `in the enactment itself` IS FALSE, `in the Act under which it is made` IS JUST TRUE)
#ASSERT     `a provision of this Act applies to an enactment` (`Where a contrary intention appears` WITH `in this Act` IS FALSE, `in the enactment itself` IS FALSE, `in the Act under which it is made` IS JUST FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `a provision of this Act applies to an enactment` (`Where a contrary intention appears` WITH `in this Act` IS TRUE,  `in the enactment itself` IS TRUE,  `in the Act under which it is made` IS JUST TRUE)

§ `Section 4(2): provisions about other Acts also apply to this Act unless the contrary intention appears in this Act`

#ASSERT     `a provision of this Act that relates to other Acts applies also to this Act` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `a provision of this Act that relates to other Acts applies also to this Act` TRUE

§ `Section 5: construing a provision that is obscure, ambiguous or absurd (not a penal or other sanction)`

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of enactment`
      sanction IS A BOOLEAN
      ambiguous IS A BOOLEAN
      absurd IS A BOOLEAN
      `fails the plain intention` IS A BOOLEAN
      ascertained IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The provision to be construed`
`a provision found in` k `, with these facts` sanction ambiguous absurd `fails the plain intention` ascertained MEANS
    `The provision to be construed` WITH
        `where it is found`                                                         IS k
        `it relates to the imposition of a penal or other sanction`                 IS sanction
        `it is obscure or ambiguous`                                                IS ambiguous
        `on a literal interpretation it would be absurd`                            IS absurd
        `on a literal interpretation it would fail to reflect the plain intention`  IS `fails the plain intention`
        `the plain intention can be ascertained`                                    IS ascertained

-- each of the three triggers alone, in an Act of the Oireachtas
#ASSERT `what section 5 directs about` (`a provision found in` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `, with these facts` FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `construe to reflect the plain intention` `the Oireachtas`
#ASSERT `what section 5 directs about` (`a provision found in` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `, with these facts` FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `construe to reflect the plain intention` `the Oireachtas`
#ASSERT `what section 5 directs about` (`a provision found in` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `, with these facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  TRUE) EQUALS `construe to reflect the plain intention` `the Oireachtas`
-- whose intention, for each kind
#ASSERT `what section 5 directs about` (`a provision found in` `a statute of Saorstat Eireann continued in force` `, with these facts` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `construe to reflect the plain intention` `the parliament concerned`
#ASSERT `what section 5 directs about` (`a provision found in` `a statutory instrument` `, with these facts` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `construe to reflect the plain intention` `the maker of the instrument`
-- a penal or other sanction takes the provision out of the section, whatever else is true
#ASSERT `what section 5 directs about` (`a provision found in` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `, with these facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `section 5 does not apply`
#ASSERT `what section 5 directs about` (`a provision found in` `a statutory instrument` `, with these facts` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `section 5 does not apply`
-- none of the triggers: the section does not apply
#ASSERT `what section 5 directs about` (`a provision found in` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `, with these facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `section 5 does not apply`
-- a trigger but no plain intention can be ascertained: the section gives no direction
#ASSERT `what section 5 directs about` (`a provision found in` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `, with these facts` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `section 5 gives no direction because the plain intention cannot be ascertained`
#ASSERT `what section 5 directs about` (`a provision found in` `a statutory instrument` `, with these facts` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `section 5 gives no direction because the plain intention cannot be ascertained`
-- no trigger and no plain intention: the section does not apply (the trigger is tested first)
#ASSERT `what section 5 directs about` (`a provision found in` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `, with these facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `section 5 does not apply`
-- the results are distinct values, so the assertions above are not satisfied by accident
#ASSERT NOT (`construe to reflect the plain intention` `the Oireachtas`) EQUALS `construe to reflect the plain intention` `the maker of the instrument`

§ `Section 6: a court may make allowance for a change since the passing or making, so far as the text, purpose and context permit`

GIVEN changed IS A DATE
      passed IS A DATE
      relevant IS A BOOLEAN
      permit IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A change since a provision was made`
`a change on` changed `to a provision passed or made on` passed `, relevant` relevant `, permitted` permit MEANS
    `A change since a provision was made` WITH
        `the day the Act was passed or the instrument was made` IS passed
        `the day of the change`                                  IS changed
        `the change is in the law, social conditions, technology, the meaning of words used, or another relevant matter` IS relevant
        `the text, purpose and context of the provision permit the allowance` IS permit

#ASSERT     `a court may make allowance for the change in construing the provision` (`a change on` (YMD 2026 3 11) `to a provision passed or made on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, relevant` TRUE `, permitted` TRUE)
#ASSERT     `a court may make allowance for the change in construing the provision` (`a change on` (YMD 2030 1 1)  `to a provision passed or made on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, relevant` TRUE `, permitted` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `a court may make allowance for the change in construing the provision` (`a change on` (YMD 2026 3 9)  `to a provision passed or made on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, relevant` TRUE `, permitted` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `a court may make allowance for the change in construing the provision` (`a change on` (YMD 2026 3 11) `to a provision passed or made on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, relevant` FALSE `, permitted` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `a court may make allowance for the change in construing the provision` (`a change on` (YMD 2026 3 11) `to a provision passed or made on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, relevant` TRUE `, permitted` FALSE)
-- the very day: the text says "since", and does not say whether the day itself counts
#ASSERT REFUSED `a court may make allowance for the change in construing the provision` (`a change on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `to a provision passed or made on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, relevant` TRUE `, permitted` TRUE) BECAUSE "section 6 does not say whether a change on the very day of the passing or making is a change since that day"
-- but a change that is not relevant, or not permitted, fails whichever day it is
#ASSERT NOT `a court may make allowance for the change in construing the provision` (`a change on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `to a provision passed or made on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, relevant` FALSE `, permitted` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `a court may make allowance for the change in construing the provision` (`a change on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `to a provision passed or made on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, relevant` TRUE `, permitted` FALSE)

§ `Section 7(1): matters that accompany the signed text, notwithstanding section 18(g), for the purposes of section 5 or 6, in the case of an Act`

#ASSERT     `section 7(1) lets a court make use of the matter notwithstanding section 18(g)` `an Act of the Oireachtas` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT     `section 7(1) lets a court make use of the matter notwithstanding section 18(g)` `a statute of Saorstat Eireann continued in force` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 7(1) lets a court make use of the matter notwithstanding section 18(g)` `an Act of the Oireachtas` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 7(1) lets a court make use of the matter notwithstanding section 18(g)` `an Act of the Oireachtas` TRUE FALSE
-- the section speaks of "a provision of an Act", so it gives a statutory instrument nothing
#ASSERT NOT `section 7(1) lets a court make use of the matter notwithstanding section 18(g)` `a statutory instrument` TRUE TRUE

§ `Section 7(2): the presumption holds until the contrary is shown`

#ASSERT     `it is presumed that the copy is a copy of the text to which section 7(1) relates` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `it is presumed that the copy is a copy of the text to which section 7(1) relates` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `it is presumed that the copy is a copy of the text to which section 7(1) relates` FALSE FALSE

§ `Section 8: summary proceedings by a specified person`

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts for section 8`
`the facts for section 8` a b c d e MEANS
    `Facts for section 8` WITH
        `the first Act or portion of an Act provides that summary proceedings for offences under it may be prosecuted by a specified person` IS a
        `it is subsequently read together as one with a provision of another Act`                                                          IS b
        `an offence is created under that provision which can be prosecuted in a summary manner`                                           IS c
        `no express power is given to the specified person to so prosecute`                                                                IS d
        `some other person is authorised by that other Act to bring such proceedings`                                                      IS e

#ASSERT     `section 8 lets the specified person bring summary proceedings for the offence` (`the facts for section 8` TRUE  TRUE  TRUE  TRUE  FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `section 8 lets the specified person bring summary proceedings for the offence` (`the facts for section 8` FALSE TRUE  TRUE  TRUE  FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `section 8 lets the specified person bring summary proceedings for the offence` (`the facts for section 8` TRUE  FALSE TRUE  TRUE  FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `section 8 lets the specified person bring summary proceedings for the offence` (`the facts for section 8` TRUE  TRUE  FALSE TRUE  FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `section 8 lets the specified person bring summary proceedings for the offence` (`the facts for section 8` TRUE  TRUE  TRUE  FALSE FALSE)
-- "unless some other person is authorised by that other Act to bring such proceedings"
#ASSERT NOT `section 8 lets the specified person bring summary proceedings for the offence` (`the facts for section 8` TRUE  TRUE  TRUE  TRUE  TRUE)

§ `Section 9: a reference to a Part or a section is read as a reference to the enactment's; to a subsection or paragraph, the provision's`

#ASSERT `a reference to a division is read as a reference to a division of` Part       EQUALS `a division of the enactment in which the reference occurs`
#ASSERT `a reference to a division is read as a reference to a division of` Chapter    EQUALS `a division of the enactment in which the reference occurs`
#ASSERT `a reference to a division is read as a reference to a division of` section    EQUALS `a division of the enactment in which the reference occurs`
#ASSERT `a reference to a division is read as a reference to a division of` Schedule   EQUALS `a division of the enactment in which the reference occurs`
#ASSERT `a reference to a division is read as a reference to a division of` subsection EQUALS `a division of the provision in which the reference occurs`
#ASSERT `a reference to a division is read as a reference to a division of` paragraph  EQUALS `a division of the provision in which the reference occurs`
#ASSERT `a reference to a division is read as a reference to a division of` subparagraph EQUALS `a division of the provision in which the reference occurs`
#ASSERT `a reference to a division is read as a reference to a division of` clause     EQUALS `a division of the provision in which the reference occurs`
#ASSERT `a reference to a division is read as a reference to a division of` subclause  EQUALS `a division of the provision in which the reference occurs`
#ASSERT `a reference to a division is read as a reference to a division of` article    EQUALS `a division of the provision in which the reference occurs`
#ASSERT `a reference to a division is read as a reference to a division of` subarticle EQUALS `a division of the provision in which the reference occurs`
#ASSERT REFUSED `a reference to a division is read as a reference to a division of` `a division with another name` BECAUSE "section 9 does not say which kind of division a division with another name is"

§ `Section 11: examples`

#ASSERT `the effect of an example under the heading` Sampla   `, included as stated by` TRUE EQUALS `the example is not exhaustive of the provision and may extend, but does not limit, its meaning`
#ASSERT `the effect of an example under the heading` Samplai  `, included as stated by` TRUE EQUALS `the example is not exhaustive of the provision and may extend, but does not limit, its meaning`
#ASSERT `the effect of an example under the heading` Example  `, included as stated by` TRUE EQUALS `the example is not exhaustive of the provision and may extend, but does not limit, its meaning`
#ASSERT `the effect of an example under the heading` Examples `, included as stated by` TRUE EQUALS `the example is not exhaustive of the provision and may extend, but does not limit, its meaning`
-- the position matters: not at the end of the provision or in a schedule relating to it
#ASSERT `the effect of an example under the heading` Example  `, included as stated by` FALSE EQUALS `section 11 does not apply`
-- another heading
#ASSERT `the effect of an example under the heading` `some other heading` `, included as stated by` TRUE EQUALS `section 11 does not apply`
#ASSERT `the heading is one the section names` Samplai
#ASSERT NOT `the heading is one the section names` `some other heading`

§ `Section 12: a deviation from a prescribed form does not invalidate it if it does not materially affect substance OR is not misleading`

#ASSERT     `section 12 saves the form used` TRUE TRUE  TRUE
#ASSERT     `section 12 saves the form used` TRUE TRUE  FALSE
#ASSERT     `section 12 saves the form used` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 12 saves the form used` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 12 saves the form used` FALSE TRUE TRUE

§ `Section 13: an Act is a public document and shall be judicially noticed`

#ASSERT `it is a public document that shall be judicially noticed` `an Act of the Oireachtas`
#ASSERT `it is a public document that shall be judicially noticed` `a statute of Saorstat Eireann continued in force`
#ASSERT REFUSED `it is a public document that shall be judicially noticed` `a statutory instrument` BECAUSE "section 13 says nothing about a statutory instrument"

§ `Section 14(1): how an Act may be cited`

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about an Act for citing it`
`the facts for citing` a b c MEANS
    `Facts about an Act for citing it` WITH
        `citing it by number and year is appropriate`                                                              IS a
        `it was passed prior to the enactment of the Constitution of the Irish Free State (Saorstat Eireann) Act 1922` IS b
        `there was more than one parliamentary session in the same regnal year`                                    IS c

#ASSERT `section 14(1) lets an Act be cited` `by the long title` `, given` (`the facts for citing` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `section 14(1) lets an Act be cited` `by the short title` `, given` (`the facts for citing` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT     `section 14(1) lets an Act be cited` `by the consecutive number of the Act in the calendar year and the calendar year in which it was passed` `, given` (`the facts for citing` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `section 14(1) lets an Act be cited` `by the consecutive number of the Act in the calendar year and the calendar year in which it was passed` `, given` (`the facts for citing` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT     `section 14(1) lets an Act be cited` `by its regnal year and chapter number` `, given` (`the facts for citing` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `section 14(1) lets an Act be cited` `by its regnal year and chapter number` `, given` (`the facts for citing` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `section 14(1) lets an Act be cited` `by its regnal year and chapter number` `, given` (`the facts for citing` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT     `section 14(1) lets an Act be cited` `by its regnal year, chapter number and the session concerned` `, given` (`the facts for citing` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `section 14(1) lets an Act be cited` `by its regnal year, chapter number and the session concerned` `, given` (`the facts for citing` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `section 14(1) lets an Act be cited` `by its regnal year, chapter number and the session concerned` `, given` (`the facts for citing` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
